{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a sharp price spike followed by immediate reversal (e.g., Example 4), the model's upward forecast is severely biased; apply a negative correction factor of -15% to -20% for the first 7 days post-spike.",
    "If sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (0.20-0.33) amidst otherwise neutral/zero sentiment, the model overestimates momentum and should be reduced by 5-8 points per day until sentiment returns to zero.",
    "In volatile regimes with high intraday swings (Example 1 & 4), the model exhibits significant mean reversion lag; forecasts that trend linearly upward during a consolidation phase must be corrected downward by 10% if the true outcome fails to sustain the initial spike.",
    "When the last 3 days of history show a clear downtrend but sentiment remains neutral, the model's flat-to-slight-upward forecast is biased high; apply a correction of -2 to -4 EUR/day until price action confirms a new trend direction.",
    "For horizons exceeding 15 days in Example 5 style volatility, the model consistently underestimates mean reversion risk; reduce long-term forecasts by 8-10% relative to the initial historical average."
  ]
}
